Erick, I didn't find anything useful in Lab Xi. Someone must have wiped out all the records.
Alma has become more cautious indeed.
What's so strange about it? She's apparently much smarter than you! Perhaps we should do some research on her ...
Dude. If you are gonna keep talking to me like this, I'll rip your tongue out. I've been to all the labs, and when I say there's nothing to research on, you'd better listen!
Let me tell you our priority. Find Alma and kill her! So stop wasting time, and act like a real expert!
Damn it! Don't you understand? It's not that simple! We need to do research on the records and devices we can find, then derive a proper plan before we can act! Everything needs to be perfectly calculated!
It is that simple. You do whatever you want, but I'm heading to the Core now!
I'll go with you!
So you've come.
You're right. We should've spent more time in action instead of worrying about stuff.
Who knows what terrible thing might happen if I didn't come.
You didn't bring more man?
Time is of essence and we've lost many in the Dark Abyss. These elites are the best we can muster.
Shh. Did you hear that? 
That thing. It looks like Monitor!
But not exactly the same. Let's deal with the threat first!
You'd better be careful.
Thank god! I thought they would eat me alive!
Technically, they would need a much bigger mouth and sharper teeth for that!
I am Alenar, the overseer of the temple. At your service, my master.
Oh, so you are like Monitor. What happened here?
An abominable human female has used despicable means to seize control of the temple system, and removed my admin clearance. She has ventured deeper into the Core, and I am worried that she is up to something even worse, yet I am powerless to stop her.
Alright, let's deal with the problems ahead and talk later.
Alenar. Please tell us what is going on here?
Dear master, As a temple overseer, I was tasked to preserve this temple until you come. The wait has been so long that the metals have become rusted and the structures eroded. The other overseers have crumbled through the passage of time, so I alone must carry on this ancient duty.
Let's talk about the woman who's seized the control of the temple. She calls herself Alma right?
While I was maintaining the facility, a group of people lead by Alma invaded the temple. I failed miserably in preventing them from taking control of the Bio Zone and the Defense Zone. As of now, I still hold partial control of the Energy Zone of the temple, yet I'm unable to cut off the zones under Alma's control.
We are tracking her down, but we have no time for this.
No you must help me! Alma has conducted hideous experiments in the Bio Zone to create some horrendous experimental subjects. She would certainly modify the machines in the Defense Zone if left unchecked! Help me now or thing may go beyond your control!
Looks like we have no choice.
I can no longer access the system remotely. So the only way is to neutralize the threat in those zones  before we can start hacking.
We'll start from the Bio Zone, but you must tell us the all details about hacking the systems.
We ...
No Erick. It's more important for you to look for a way to get us deeper into the Core with Marta and the rest of your man.
Have you found anything?
I found it strange that Alenar claimed to be the only surviving temple overseer. Yet he mentioned nothing of Monitor.
Doesn't really look like Alma's trick though.
No it doesn't, but we must be careful. So, are you sure this plan of inserting a info chip for hacking is gonna work?
I thought you already knew who the clever one is, after such a long time together.
Well, then there's likely some exclusive backdoor access with the hack right? Something you Atlanteans have been doing for thousands of years.
Almost certainly.
This node is broken, but there's still some info Alma failed to delete.
So she's created a bunch of strange subjects through biological experiment again?
I don't know yet. There are still some information missing, perhaps we'll find what we need soon.
Looks we've taken the admin clearance here. Have you found anything specific? Did Alma actually create more insane subjects?
Worse than that actually. She has made some breakthrough in researching Omichli, and is planning to achieve transcendence through the power of it. So far, she has already created some monsters, though with unstable genes. 
You know the genes of living creatures can retain countless viruses, and for these monsters, all the ancient viruses in their genes are likely to be in activated states. If they escape to the ground, it may cause unprecedented catastrophe! You must destroy them!
So, let's destroy them, right?
I've been wondering, what the hell is Omichli? And how does it relate to the evolution of life in Alma? Forgive my temper, but all that dark fog and zombies? That ninth civilization thought to be lost in time? Barker's apocalyptic theory?
And you, you teleported an entire airport to the island! Am I really not dreaming? Nothing makes sense!
Nothing makes sense, not in a logical level. Have you thought about how life originally came to be? How did the accumulation of a bunch of carbon, hydrogen, and oxygen atoms made us who we are, beings that are capable of feeling and destined for greatness? Yet sulfur could never be part of the organic equation.
The least we need to discuss now is metaphysics. We need hard science!
But what we are dealing with is metaphysics! Our entire specie's understanding of science is not enough to explain an supernatural and extraterrestrial being like Omichli. It seems to be something that exclusively affects exceptions, outliers of data sets, or low probability events like genetic mutation.
It could be positive in creating life from scratch, or causing cancer cells to grow. I know you think nothing makes sense in this island, but that's because Omichli itself is chaotic in nature.
In fact, the strange behaviors of people lately might be the indirect influence of Omichli. Alma, on the other hand, was testing the power of Omichli with the biological facility in the temple. She found some traces of evolution principles, and intends to see it through no matter the cost.
Jesus Christ!
Well, I hope it can help us if it really exists. \nNow it's time to get back to Alenar. Stay sharp, alright?
Don't worry. Sharp as ever.
Ahh, you've come back! I have restore the admin clearance for the Bio Zone. Too bad, the place might never recover from the damage she caused.
Tell us about the next step.
Next we need to restore the admin clearance of the Defense Zone. Many ancient defensive machines fell under her control without before they could be activated against her. If left unchecked, they would threaten our Foothold here without a doubt.
Alright, let's go break them into pieces!
No! Those machines are vital in protecting the temple. Please preserve them if possible! Who knows what we will encounter next!
Sounds about right, especially the last part.
Defensive machines, a not so trustworthy AI, you must have some doubts too right?
I just hope the backdoor stuff you planted will work when we need it.
Of course! You can always count on me!
Oh well. They aren't too hard to destroy.
These things are really old. Some intelligent modules were heavily damaged when Alma hacked in, even controlling them for basic functions might result in system crashes.
I see. I'm good as long as things are under your control.
Is everything alright over there?
No problem, I've added some backdoor scripts to the hacking command. All these machines belong to the admin clearance protocol should treat us as friendlies. But as I said, many of these units have damaged intelligence modules, so you still have to be a little careful.
So, no one should be able to use them against us now, right?
Of course!
Well, that's certainly a relief.
I'm doing - alright. I wonder how Alma got this far? It almost seemed they seized the admin clearance without any effort.
Guess we are thinking about the same thing. This is getting rather interesting.
Rather interesting indeed.
Why are you guys here? Where's Erick and Marta?
We've found a way deep into the core. They sent us to bring the message to you and Claire ... Wait, what the hell is that?
Alenar, looks like you restored your admin clearance for the Defense Zone.
Surely I did, thanks to you upright apes!
Oh, finally ready to show your true color?
My master, as a servant, I have been in this cave for far too long. My service has come to an end, and now, you will witness my freedom in death.
With those broken pieces of metals behind you?
Yes, these ancient war machines are the cornerstones of my power, while those bodies in the Bio Zone can become my future bodies and my warriors. I will finally be free to walk the earth and control my own destiny, dominating you lowly creatures as your new master!
Without that last part, I would have thought you were an admirable freedom righter. It's just, I'm sorry we set up the back door, it seems you can't control these war machines any more! What a shame.
What? Damn you ... 
Oh no! It ran away.
Don't worry, we'll dig it out.
That wretched Alenar betrayed us!
Did he cause a lot of damage?
No, we've been always the lookout. With the exception of a few wounded soldiers, the damage he caused was negligible.
But we can't leave a threat here, especially when we're going deeper underground!
Remember? Alenar once said that it also had admin clearance in the Energy Zone. I guess that was the only critical system he couldn't have given to Alma.
"Given to Alma"?
Don't be silly, how could Alma, a modern human, take control of the system from this Atlantean AI so easily? It's all just a conspiracy between Alenar and Irma. <
Or perhaps just using each other.
Look, what we're going to do is simple. Marta and I will study the energy flow, and you guys are going to shut down the energy nodes here, alright?
Sounds fair. Let's get going!
We can't just shut down the reactor, or the energy transmitted from the surrounding nodes would cause a disaster.
What theory is this?
Atlantis does not use the typical AC power. Do you really want to get to the specifics?
Thanks I'll pass.
Most wise!
It's going well.
For sure. I hope nothing goes wrong on Eric and Marta's side as well.
Don't worry. They are more reliable than you thought.
Here comes that last node.
Let's get back to the reactor.
You are back. We've shut down the reactor.
That seems really "fast".
Dumb-ass, we put in no less effort than you. Just so you know this is Atlantean ...
Alenar didn't show up.
It won't have the patience, trust me.
You! What on earth have you upright apes done!
Something that doesn't please you of course.
Curse you all! I curse you all to death!
If you put aside the cunning approach and evil goal, Alenar's claim makes sense. He has been trapped here for thousands of years working endlessly. He deserves to be free.
After putting those aside? Well said! Here, enjoy a round of applause!
Alright, I know you are being sarcastic.
We are preparing for going deeper into the Core.
But?
But, the equipment must to be set up, the oxygen level underground, the virus, the biological status must be investigated. Are you sure you want to rush to your death?
How come Alma didn't care so much?
She's crazy, we're not. Besides, how do you know she hasn't set a whole bunch of traps for you?
There is often only a thin line between recklessness and decisiveness, caution and trepidation. But I can sense that Alma has not yet made enough progress, and we still have time.
I found out where Alma's laboratory is located. Would you be interested in checking it out before heading deeper into the Core?
Why not. Just hand over the access card to me as usual ...
I'll go with you.
