You are here as expected! Listen, I've had a breakthrough in my research and finally found some key genes from the samples, including some retroviruses!
Hold on. What the hell is retrovirus?
Simply put, it's a type of RNA virus. During the long evolutionary process, these RNA viruses have entered the human genome and achieved a state of coexistence. In fact, about 8% of the human genome is filled with these viruses.
After analyzing the samples, I found that retroviruses in some genes were reactivated and evolved, which in turn led to the mutation of the organism. If this virus spreads, it could cause an ecological disaster with global repercussions!
Damn it, this must have been the work of Omichli! \n<Claire explained the influence of Omichli to Alenka>
Do you have any ways to solve the problem we are facing?
If it's only for the current strains of viruses, the vaccine I have just developed should work fine. But if those viruses continue to evolve, things might get out of hand rather quickly, so you better get rid of Omichli quickly.
Of course, we'll deal with Omichli. You can count on us!
<A Message from Alma>
It's still you guys I assume? My research is nearly complete with a new era about to dawn on humanity, and you are too late to do anything now. 
<A Message from Alma>
I respect your stubbornness, but know that the power of Omichli cannot be stopped. Instead of allowing humans to mutate uncontrollably, let me guide the evolution. I hope you can understand that I am doing humanity a favor.
<Another Message from Alma. Yet this time her words and handwriting seem a bit hesitant>
But ... what if I am wrong?
Perhaps Ethan's theory was right. Unfortunately he died too soon.
Alenka, do you know Alma or Erick?
<Sighing softly> I do. In fact we were all members of a scientific research team and after the shipwreck, we ended up on this island. Unfortunately we later went our separate ways because of our ideological differences.
Well, what about Ethan?
How do you know this person? He died years ago, I almost forgot about him ... Oh I see.
What's wrong?
Damn it! I should have thought about it sooner. But I don't time to explain now. Just get to Erick and tell him. Tell him Ethan might very well be right about his theory!
Alma mentioned a guy named Ethan, and Alenka wanted me to tell you Ethan might be right.
Ethan? Oh God! You are saying Ethan might be right? No! Impossible! This can't be true! Ethan was a complete idiot, and his research made no sense!
Tell us about Ethan's research please.
In our study of the anomalies on the island, Ethan proposed a theory that there was some kind of force on the island that would induce a mutation in matter, similar to the observation of quantum field. Once something is noticed by that force, it will mutate completely.
Ethan was right, that's what Omichli does! I'll explain more about it once we meet up with Marta and Baak.
The last time I heard about Ethan was when he died in accident while trying too look for something that he believed could contain that kind of power.
No, it was not an accident. He was murdered.
Monitor! How are you here?
Did you say Ethan was murdered?
Ethan discovered the device used by Atlanteans for countering Omichli. It is called the Mirror Palace. Ethan and I had a brief discussion about if before he was murdered by some AIs that betrayed their creators.
Hold on. What is Mirror Palace?
Based on Ethan's research, it was probably a device your ancestors built to counter Omichli after realizing the disaster it could bring. Even among the Temple Overseers, the Mirror Palace is considered top secret.
If the Atlanteans had a device to counter Omichli, then how did it affect the humans and creatures on the island?
It seems that the Mirror Palace device was subjected to a strong electromagnetic storm, resulting in damage to some of its components, which significantly limited its effect against Omichli. We must stop the electromagnetic storm from happening again if we want to have any chance in dealing with Omichli.
Zhu Lan of Salvation Town has already started working on this. Time is running out, so you might want to work together.
Why should we trust you?
I'll be with Monitor and analyze its algorithm. Don't worry. It'll be alright.
Zhu Lan, you've been investigating the cause of the electromagnetic energy anomaly on the island lately, right?
Yes, several of my companions and I are very concerned about this matter. We believe that the unusual surge of electromagnetic energy has caused a high number of air and sea accidents, like the cruise ship that ran aground. I am planning to go to the cruise ship to investigate the navigation records.
Great. I'll go with you.
You ... don't look so well. Is everything OK?
<You can't help but smile bitterly>\nWell, we are potentially dealing with the end of the world. Let's go, I'll explain it to you on the way.
The end of ... the world?
This is the cruise ship that ran aground. You have to be careful. There are surviving crew members here, but they're all a little out of shape.
I still find it hard to believe that the things you said.
Believe me, if all this turns out to be some bullshit nonsense, then I'll be the happiest one!
Anyway, let's go ahead and get that navigation record.
Well the records here ... are a complete mess. But at least we know Bale is the one who recorded this.
I saw this man in the Glacier, but I thought he was just an adventurer. Come on, let's go find out, hopefully he hasn't gone far.
Then let's hurry up and get going.
Hey, my friend! What brings you here?
It's been a long while, Bale. \nYou never told me you were a crew member of that stranded cruise ship.
What's there to say? The ship ran aground, monsters broke into the ship, and the crew became insane. I tried everything, but in the end I had leave for my own safety.
Listen, Bale. I need you to tell us about the electromagnetic storm that hit the cruise ship before it ran aground. It's the key to everything.
Well ... at that time, the cruise ship was hit by a strong electromagnetic storm, and the energy surge fried countless vital circuits and crippled all navigation systems, which eventually caused the cruise ship to run aground.
But as the electromagnetic storm became increasingly violent, our sensors picked up a some kind of a signal. Then storm then suddenly disappeared, as if everything was an illusion.
I used a hard drive to store that signal, only to accidentally lose it some time ago while trying to explore into the volcano. If you need it, just go to the volcano and look for it.
You are Alizée, right?
Yes. Do you have the hard drive?
How did you know about the hard drive.
<Rolling eyes with great restraint> \n Hey, don't play dumb, you know Zhu Lan will exchange messages with me, right? Now give me the hard drive quickly, and don't waste my time!
Hey, have you seen the Asian girl named Zhu Lan, please?
Oh, I just saw her heading for the beach, looking quite depressed.
The beach? Well, thank you, Damian.
You are welcome.
Why did you come here alone?
I'm just ... a little tired.
But you seem anxious.
I've always wondered if what you said was true, that would mean there was an ancient being far beyond our comprehension? And it could destroy us all.
Do we really stand a chance against that? Will we be able to get back to our normal life?
I'm scared, terrified in fact. I wish I was like you, always brave and fearless.
I'll tell you a secret. I'm also scared, scared of death, scared of not being able to go home, that's why I fight.
You are trying to make me feel better. You don't have to do this. I just want to be alone for a little bit.
Come, take a sip of this.
<Taking a sip of Dark Wolf Brew>\ncough cough ... this ... what the hell is this? It's really spicy!
Feeling a bit pumped up now?
Thank you, I know you want to encourage me to pull myself together, I'm just too weak.
I know how you feel. Everyone is struggling to survive here, but that doesn't stop us from having hope. If something is right, then do it, no matter how hard it is.
All of us will die eventually, but when it happens, I hope I won't regret wasting my time for nothing.
You are right, I need to be strong. Let's go find Alizée. Hopefully she's got some leads already.
Here you are. I analyzed the electromagnetic storm data in the hard drive, and there is no doubt that it has a strong artificial signal signature. However, regarding the strange signal at the end of the record, I have no clue for the time being.
So, is there anything we can do now?
Arthur sent a message that he detected a strange energy surge over in the Wasteland and suspected that it was related to the electromagnetic storm you mentioned.
Zhu Lan, what brings you here? It can be a bit dangerous here.
I'm not afraid, and I think I can help.
Well, we do need people here.
Did you find anything? Arthur?
Some devices with high energy reactions that shouldn't have been here.
According to Alizée's theory, these energy devices combined cause a strong electromagnetic storm if all their energy are released at the same time.
Where did these things come from? Is there some kind of a a production line on this island?
I have a few suspicions. We'd better split up the scouting to save time. I'll go with Zhu Lan to scout out the ORU territory, while you'll head to Lab Theta.
A high energy reactor, but it was damaged.
More damaged devices of the same kind. Yet the production line is no where to be seen.
We discovered some strange devices that contained alarming amounts of energy. We tried to dismantle them, but the resulting energy leak caused a disaster.
Damn it. Those devices aren't made by ORU lab researchers!
What happened here? Is Zhu Lan injured?
We've been attacked by a bunch of armed robots! I think they were controlled by an floating orb robot. I managed to deal with them, but the orb robot got away and Zhu Lan was injured in combat!
The Temple Overseer traitors! I knew it was them! 
I'll take Zhu Lan to Salvation Town. Help us find some medicine alright? Please be quick or she won't make it!
Here are the meds. How's Zhu Lan?
She's still alive. Good thing Alizée is looking after her. I'm sure she'll be OK with the meds. Oh yeah, this is my friend Neva. We gotta continue tracking down the storm soon!
But we lost all the clues.
Not all of them. We managed identify another abnormality in the Highland while you were busy.
Whatever created these, it must be quite anxious right now!
So are we my friend.
This isn't good! According to the readings, the energy level is surging here!
What should we do?
There has to be some energy generators in this area. We must to find them!
This must be one of them!
Have you thought of a way to destroy it?
As a warrior, destruction is my specialty! And I always carry some explosives with me. Let's split up and blow them up to pieces!
Let's not be hasty and think it through for a bit. Who knows if the explosion might unleash all the energy stored in the generator?
But that didn't happen, did it? And we prevented the electromagnetic storm from happening again.
I doubt it. The energy level nearby did not go down. There must be more energy generators around.
Damn it! Then let's find them all and blow them all!
The AI traitor has spotted our actions. Surely they will rise their alert level.
Then destroy them all! Let's move!
This one seems rather different from the others.
Well, it is not an energy generator but a poly-energy blasting device! I got it! All the energy from those generators will converge over here to create an immensely powerful energy blast, which then forms the electromagnetic storm!
Looks like we made it just in time. Once we blow this up, we should be able to take a breather.
Have you brought enough explosives?
You bet I have!
Listen Arthur. We probably need to have a conversation after this.
