Because of you, Claire. I can't stand idly by while you are on a dangerous adventure!
Stop, Jack. We talked about this before. We both know you are not my dad.
But you are Jane's daughter. That means I'll help no matter what.
Woof!
Look, even Riley agrees!
Very touching indeed.
Alma!
How dare you show up in front of us, Alma! You killed Jane! 
Strictly speaking. I didn't. Her death was a tragedy that none of us wanted to see.
Shut up! B**ch!
Listen up, you naive folks. How many tragedies do you think have happened on this island? And how many are happening around the world right now? You don't know a thing!
But now we have a chance. Embrace Omichli and use its power to transform all of humanity. Only then will we control our own destinies and achieve true freedom!
Enough! No more preaching of your questionable theory! I'm going to kill you now and bring justice to Jane!
Alright. You've made your choice. Kill them!
Damn it! She ran way, we must hurry up and...
Calm down, Jack!
I cant calm down!
Use your brain! Do you want us to rush into a trap and put Claire in danger?
Woof woof!
Yeah, you have point. I shouldn't be so impulsive, but we can't let Alma escape, right?"
Very well, We must be more cautious for Alma has been operating here for a while.
Wretched followers of Alma!
As expected, she's got the defenses fully set up. Careful now!
Awoooo!
Hang on! The bridge is rigged with high voltage!
Fuck!
Ambush, ambush!
How can we pass this bridge?
I noticed a control console not far from here. Maybe we should go over there and try our luck.
I'll stay here and make sure Alma's followers don't come through again.
Okay, we'll be back soon.
Damn it, this thing is wrecked.
Isn't there any way we can figure this out?
There's nothing I can do, Alma's followers have completely wrecked this area.
Well, guess we'll have to find another way.
Morpheus, good to see you here.
Wearing a steel mask doesn't make me cold like steel. We come to help you solve the problems.
Arthur has already stopped Alma's technician on the northern platform from destroying the control hub. Once we take care of some technical issues, we can disable the high voltage on the bridge.
Then what are we waiting for? Let's hurry up and go!
Arthur, did you just used a disguise?
Well, it's just a simple trick of my past, but it seems like we don't have much time, Alma's followers will be here soon.
Then we'll take them down.
Aha! I love it when adrenaline rushes through my veins!
So, what's next?
Simple. There are two keys for console, each held by one of Alma's followers.
So, we'll just take them out, grab the keys, and disable the high voltage on the console?
Precisely!
Claire, I'm about to activate the device. You've got this?
Absolutely! Even though I'm not sure how it works, it's like part of my genes know how to control these devices, like instincts!
Jack, the high voltage is longer on the bridge.
I could tell. cough ...
Did you get hurt?
We were attacked, and Jack was incredibly brave.
Now that bridge is unrigged, let's ...
Jack, you can't go with them. Your injury will be a burden to Claire.
What the hell are you talking about!
That's a fact. Look, we all know how much responsibility the survivor and Claire are carrying, and I won't let your injury get in the way.
You can't keep me away from this, Morpheus!
Listen to my words, Jack. Leave the rest to us. We'll seek vengeance from Alma and save this world from Omichli's grasp
<Unwilling to accept the reality, Jack roared with a sense of frustration> You all better come back in one piece! Do you hear me? In one piece!
Since Alma doesn't want us to cross the bridge, can we assume that she still has some secrets hidden here?
That's what I thought, but I doubt anyone here can tell us.
Not necessarily. Temple overseers are AIs, and they tend to store vast amounts of data.
No wonder there are so many consoles here.
Based on the Temple Overseer's records, Alma is ... attempting to communicate with Omichli?
Does that even work?
Of course not! My ancestors did the same thing, but eventually they realized Omichli was so capricious in words, and you might as well consider it a lunatic.
Yet, that's exactly what Alma is.
Precisely what frightens me the most! That's all we have from this terminal, we should find another one.
Why didn't Atlanteans connect these terminals to a network to share information?
Security? Stubbornness? Stupidity? You are free to have your own opinion.
I can tell from your face that things aren't looking so good.
You're right. Alma is repeating the mistake that Atlanteans made before. She's seeking power from Omichli, who in turn granted her some. Now, Alma is using that power to advance the so-called "Human Evolution"!
And then the dormant virus in human RNA will also evolve and cause an outbreak? You warned us about that.
It's worse than that. Alma has also taken this into consideration. She plans to keep advancing human evolution until it eventually overpowers the virus's evolution, and this process will be chaotic and unpredictable!
Haven't you realized what this means? If we humans starts to undergo constant evolutions and mutations, how could you even define who we are?
You mean... my god! In that case, the greatest threat to mankind will not be virus, but the concept of our very existence?
Let's put this aside for later. Now, we have to deal with the trouble at hand!
Jesus Christ! Alma's followers are indeed everywhere, aren't there?
And there's even worse to come!
<Informed Erick and others of your findings>
No ... this is sheer madness!
I thought you knew already.
We must change our plan!
