I'm afraid you have no other choice. The Mirror Palace that imprisons Omichli has been severely damaged. If left unattended, the consequences for humanity might be worse than entrusting it to Alma's "controlled evolution".
But you could be another Alma.
No... she couldn't possibly be the another Alma. I... I might have an idea about her secret. Trust me, it should indeed be kept a secret.
You? Another Atlantean prophecy of yours?
Enough, since we have no choice, we might as well take the chance and trust her.
Glad you've made the right choice.
Restoring the Mirror Palace is far from easy. Trust me, it'll take some time.
Oh, that sounds great!
Where should we start?
Let's start by stabilizing the its functionality. Here, I have crafted several devices that need to be installed at specific weak spots within the Mirror Palace.
I really hope this works.
Great, we've temporarily stabilized the palace, this should be able to sustain its functionality for a while.
Only for a while?
You don't seriously think that a few tiny devices can fully restore the greatest engineering creation of the Atlanteans, do you? Our work has just begun.
Alma! You wretched hag!
Show some respect, young one! You have no idea about the true significance of my actions.
My plane will soon come to fruition. You should step aside and not come any closer!
Or I will show no mercy!
We must find a way to get past the barrier!
Well said, but where should be begin?
To the best of my knowledge, Alizée is an expert in the field of high-energy electromagnetics. She surely has a way to solve this problem.
What brought you back? I was planning on coming to help you.
<Telling Alizée about the electromagnetic barrier>
Ah, I see. I'll make some preparations and discuss with Robert. Once that's done, you should come join us!
