Don't get any closer!
(She looks at you with suspicion.)
Thank you for saving me. These ... eh, "people"? What are these "people"? 
Just like what you saw. Come, follow me. That gun sound will attract them here. It's not safe here. 
This is what I built. Those electric fences are supposed to ... well, it might not be 100% accurate, but you can call those things: <color="#fee685">Mutants</color>. Those fences were supposed to keep those Mutants out. 
But the wreckage of the plane destroyed the fence. So now the Mutants are getting in!
Pick up that Chainsaw over there and help me do some house-cleaning!
If you are up to no good, I don't mind using this gun to finish you, along with those Mutants!
There are still many Mutants left near the Camp.
We need to fix the electric fence before it gets dark, or none of us will be doing any sleeping tonight.
I'll fix the distribution box. And you take that tool kit and fix the electric fence. Quickly!  
(She is repairing the distribution box very quickly, and the wires touched each other with sparks flying everywhere.)
Damn it! The wiring in the distribution box has been corroded! Those monsters are getting dangerously close!
See that gun on the ground? Use it to buy me some time!
I know you have many questions, but there is not much I can tell you.
We need to use this time to rest. Safe time is very short.
You're awake? Can't believe you were still able to fall asleep ... 
Well, you always need a good rest, especially in a dangerous environment.
If I didn't see you walking out of that plane with my own eyes, I'd have thought you were a spy. Well, since you didn't cause any problems yesterday, let me teach you some surviving rules here.
Look at what you're wearing! You don't stand a chance in front of those monsters. Take this hammer and collect some <color="#fee685">Rags</color> from monsters to make some clothes!
Like you said, it's not looking good ... Jane, this is Mr. Munchie. I saved him from those monsters back in their nest. He's very good at using guns. 
Very nice, we have a new member joining us. Perhaps now we are able to deal with that upcoming Mutant Horde.
Jane ... That's exactly what I wanted to say. Is there any way we can get out of here? I don't understand why you've never tried to get out of here?
(Jane's eyes flickered) Get out of here ... there should be a way, right? Well, how about we eat a coconut first? Making improvements to the Camp is the most important thing, right? (Jane suddenly held her head and curled up in pain) No, <color="#fee685">don't try to get away</color>, I can't, no ... all the people who have tried are all ... 
(Jane straightens up with a different look on her face, and a strange confusion in her voice) You are right, we need to leave. But first, we need to have some equipment to protect us. Trust me, you don't wanna see countless Mutants swimming towards you on the ocean. There are some <color="#fee685">good stuff</color> in the woods. Get them first then we can talk about what's next.
Oh, I didn't think there are any survivors besides me and Jane! Hi! My name is Claire
What is a little girl like you doing over here? Wait, you know Jane? 
More than that! I guess ... mom must have forgotten to mention me. She always forgets, not on purpose though, it's just ... 
I get it ... a Mutant Horde is coming, come back with me. But first I need to find some <color="#fee685">Materials</color> that I can use to fight those Mutants.
I know where it is! It's in the <color="#fee685">Crate</color> up ahead. That Military Chest, which was hidden by Jane, should be there. But be careful, there is a powerful boar guarding it. You need to take it out with <color="#fee685">STEALTH</color>!
TTest22
Nicely done! Pretty fast, not bad!
Well, I got what we need, that's what matters, isn't it?
Haha ... Before we go back, let's collect some wood by cutting down more trees. Jane might need them.
(Jane looks very strange) Jane ... that's right, my name is Jane! I remember now! What? What did you do? We need more hands to make some improvements to the Camp ... 
Hey! I'm back, Jane. We've gotten plenty this time! Wait? You're not feeling well again ... 
Claire, where did you go ... Oh no!! Did you spend a night out there again? Let me see, are you hurt? I'm so sorry ... 
Do worry, you know, those bad guys won't hurt me. Don't be sad, okay? Well ... let's think about something else first? I saw more monsters are coming our way earlier today.
(Jane looks at you) Looks like we have to hurry. Thank you for bringing Claire back. Your weapon seems to be worn out. Maybe try upgrading the <color="#fee685">Stone Hammer</color>. But doing so, you need to build a <color="#fee685">Workbench (Wood)</color> first, so that you can start crafting more <color="#fee685">Wood</color> for upgrading.
You have finished the tent? That's good news. Now, you have your own place to sleep.
It's been raining a lot lately, so how about we build a Rain Collector to use it as a freshwater source?
How come you have this signal gun?! Did I ... what you've heard just now, even though I'm not sure what it was, it definitely was not a plane ... 
Well ... that signal must have attracted some enemies ... I'm afraid we have to get ready to leave now.
Oh! I can use these binoculars to take a look!
Are we going to retrieve the radio? I know where it is! Jane has hid it in a very dangerous place.
For your safety, you should upgrade your weapon before we go. How about <color="#fee685">upgrade the Stone Hammer</color> again?
You should probably keep a distance from the Dark Fog. Ever since Jane inhaled some by accident, she has been phasing in and out of her mind.
I think the Dark Fog has been on this island for quite some time. I believe it came from beneath the earth.
This swamp has three ancient lamps. I'm not sure where they came from, but the Dark Fog will dissipate if you light them all.
You can use these ambers to light a fire, and make sure you don't lose them. OK, let's move!
All done! The Dark Fog is gone!
But there are some <color="#fee685">Dangerous Crocodiles</color> up ahead. Maybe you can try this!
Not bad! Now you look like a real survivor! How are you feeling? Do you feel like you're bursting with energy? Focus on that feeling and you'll become even stronger one day! Hold on, why do I know all this ... 
This radio should be in that wreckage. Let's keep moving!
Dealing with these crocodiles is becoming very difficult. They were not like this the last time I saw them ... 
The radio shouldn't be too far. But there is a huge crocodile up ahead. We need to come up with something. How about we use that rattan?
Does it work?
Nicely done!
I'll go inside and look for the radio device. Stay here and watch my back~
Haha, did you have fun on this adventure?
I hope this thing is still working. Let's head back to see Jane!
By the time I get to the camp, Jane was already gone. Is it because she thought I'm too naughty and left me ... 
(She looks at you, with a frown on her face and tears in her eyes.)
No, Jane told me she had something important to do. Don't worry, we will see her soon.
I don't need you to treat me like a child right now ... my senses are never wrong ... she left me for good this time ...
Claire, right, Jane told me that a radio can help us! Maybe she will contact us through it!
I've alway felt something special about this radio ... wait! There's a signal! It must be from Jane!
Jane taught me how to calculate coordinates ... Got the location of the signal!
Jane and I built a little boat, which is docked at the beach. If we can fix it, we should be able to set sail! Come with me.
When you're ready, let's go to Salvation Town. Jane must be waiting for us over there already. She must be!
Hello, Survivor! Welcome to Salvation Town. My name is Damien.
Here, you can trade weapons, gears, and other supplies with other survivors. You guys are welcome to look around and meet the folks.
Who are you? Did you send the signals? Have you seen a lady name Jane?
Everybody here is a survivor. Kane was the one who sent the signal. As for "Jane" ... I've never met a person with that name.
You should ask Shana. She owns a gun shop and knows pretty much everyone around this place. Go through the door, then go to your left, and you will see her. She isn't very hard to recognize.
Nice! New faces! Want to see some cool guns?
We are looking for a person. Her name is Jane. She has black hair, wears a red sweater, and she's her mom.
(Thinking) Jane ... My apologies. I have never met anyone with that name.
OK, we will go ask someone else.
Hang on! Why not purchase a gun? You know, with all these man-eating beasts hanging around out there, not to mention ... (In low voice) those Mutants are not the only ones you need to be careful of around here. I'm sure you know what I mean.
You must have received my signals! My name is Kane, and I'm the founder of Salvation Town. I also serve as the elected leader for the time being ... so, you two are here to join us?
Yeah, we hope we can have a place to rest up ...
Great! Salvation Town always welcomes new blood! To survive on this dangerous island, we must gather our strength.
Hello, have you seen Jane? She is pretty tall, has black hair, and wears a dark-red shirt ... 
I'm sorry little girl. We've never heard about the person you are looking for ... I suggest you settle down for a bit, so you can prepare well for your next step.
Hello, friend! Check out my new invention! I guarantee that you won't find this anywhere else!
Hello, are you Rex? Kane wants me to pick up some explosives for him.
Ughh, that old man again ... I really don't want to give him my stuff ... 
Fine, just take them! Make sure to find me if you ever need any gears! I will give you a great price!
This is ...?
One of the newly opened up areas near Salvation Town for survivors like you. This one belongs to you now ...
Feel free to build facilities as you see fit. But be aware, this isn't exactly a safe haven .. in fact, nowhere is completely safe on this entire island.
These explosives are ready. Here, take some and help me get rid of those Mutants for good!
Wow, I'm impressed! Someone with abilities like that is always welcomed here.
Here, we believe in unity. It helped us improve our lives. So, would you consider joining us here? This place is far safer than the other parts of the island.
We still need to find Jane ...
Little girl, this island is full of danger. You two should settle down here, so we know we can find you when we get hold of Jane.
Fine ...
So, ready to join us?\nAs soon as you are ready, I will send some people to move your <color="#8edd5c">Temporary Camp to this Survivors' Camp</color>.
This place is better than I expected. Not a trace of Dark Fog anywhere in sight!
I wish Jane can be here ...
Claire, let's settle down first ...
I'm sure your new home will only get better!
I'll need some time to find the info you guys need. In the meantime, you guys should go take a look around Salvation Town and meet your new friends.
Once you build your home to a certain point, you can seek out the farmer Herman to expand your space! That guy claims to be the most powerful man in the town. Perhaps he can teach you a few things.
New friends! Welcome! I heard you guys helped us with the Mutant problem! We owe you big time!
If you join a Camp, you can participate in Camp Events with other survivors. Come and see me when you want to expand your Camp.
I have an advice. There's a <color=#fee685>Daily Challenge</color> in Salvation Town. You should actively participate in it to make yourself stronger.
Well done! It seems you have gotten good at Daily Challenges.
What? Improving too slowly? OK, not far from this place lays an "Ancient Training Ground." I heard it's the place where all the ancient warriors have trained.
You should visit the ancient training ground every day to train yourself, obtain exp, and earn various rewards! Let's see if you have the courage.
I have some good news for you guys!
I received some signals, which are a lot different from the ones I received before. They are on pace and rapid, similar to that of morse code. I think this has something to do with the person you guys are looking for.
Jane! It has to be her! Where is the signal coming from?
The signals should be from that ship, which is located next to the shore. The problem is a thick Dark Fog has covered that region, and you can only get there by going through the Shoal.
The Shoal is full of mutated creatures, so you should get well-prepared before heading out.
Ok. Thank you!
Ahhh ... what a disaster! It was all my fault ... I was too reckless ... 
The monsters on this island are more vicious than expected. We should collect some cassowary furs. We can use them to make some better clothes.
Look! Dark Fog is coming out of those holes!
We must find a way to block them, or more animals will be infected!
Nicely done! I hope we can have an easier time for the rest of the way ... 
Let's move closer to the sea, and block all the fumaroles on our way there.
The Dark Fog is everywhere! It's no wonder that the beasts here are so savage ... 
Wait a minute, I see something! Let's go over there.
Something happened to this place ... I don't have a good feeling about this ... 
It's Jane's! Did she run into some kind of danger?
(She is getting anxious, and tears are starting to drip from her eyes ... )
Claire, calm down. Jane knows how to protect herself. You should know that.
I just wish I can see her immediately, like nothing has ever happened. Let's go to that ship!
Woot ... That was close! There are more and more monsters!
Darn it! The bridge is destroyed. Maybe we should get some wood to restore it.
OK! These materials are enough! I think it's sturdy enough to support the two of us.
Do you see that? There's a pack of mutated boars on the other side! Let's make some extra preparations, and I'll build the bridge once you are ready.
Let's keep going and find Jane!
Jane's on this ship? Let me think of a way for us to get inside ... 
I almost forgot! I know how to make climbing ropes. Let's hurry up and gather the materials I need!
Those are the materials I need! This will only take a moment.
I sense threats inside cargo. Let's do our best not to disturb the "people" inside.
I do wish to find Jane, but we should do some training and preparation before we get on that ship. Let's see if Kane has any ideas.
It looks like you've prepared sufficiently for this. It's time to embark on a new adventure!
In this dangerous world, it isn't a bad thing to accumulate more practical experience.
Challenge the <color="#8edd5c">"Joint Hunt"</color> with other survivors. Maybe you'll reap some new rewards.
Who ... who's there?
(A horrific cry of a man comes from the dark cabin. He stands up slowly with a frightened and despairing look ... )
A living person! Nice! What happened to this ship? Why are all the sailors acting like raged up monkeys?
Our ship must have been cursed ... they suddenly turned ... biting, chasing, and eating all the ones that weren't mutated ...
I was the second officer of this ship. Can you help me look in the management room? Someone might still be alive in there ... if not ... you know what to do ... 
Did I step on something?
(Claire picks up a torn piece of paper from the ground.)
It says, "The engine has stopped working for two days. We are completely trapped! More and more people are turning into savage beasts ... "
And there's more, "The Second Officer locked us in a room, so there's no way out ... I don’t know how much longer this cabinet can protect me ... from those monsters ... "
I don't think he survived ...
Anyone ... alive?
We freed them from the pain. You were the one that damned them into this fate.
No one left? But ... but if I didn't lock that door, more people would have died.
What are you talking about? Look around, there's no one alive!
It was all my fault ... I admit that ... but can you retrieve something from the storage room for me? I need to atone my sin ... 
What! Did he kill himself?
(Claire slowly walks toward the man’s corpse and then sees a neatly folded paper and something that looks to be a key card.)
What does the note say?
Thank you for "freeing" my crew. I'm sorry for breaking my promise, but I can't face the fact that I'm partially responsible for their death ... You guys have found my hidden biscuit. There isn't much food left on the ship, so I want to use it to help the ones that are still alive ... 
The Captain is trapped in the Break Room. I don't know why you guys are on the ship, but if he is still alive, he should be able to tell you what you wish to know.
Let's go find the Captain in the Break Room, Claire.
Take this, it's what I found along the way. It should help us move around faster...
You see it too, right?
That wire comes out of that room and leads to the control room.
I can't wait any longer! I haven't heard from the research team since they got off this ship! Monsters, everyone turned into monsters! Wait! I ... Who am I!!!!
Are you the Captain? Have you seen a lady with dark-brown hair in a red sweater?
Ca ... captain? That's right! I'm the captain! Are you guys the rescue team?
Of course not! Can you tell us what happened here?
My head ... it hurts ... I need some painkillers ... 
There's something wrong with the captain ...
Let's hurry and get some Painkillers. I need to ask him about Jane!
I thought I died ... Why am I here? Was it all just a dream?
We got the medicine, Captain!
I'm starving ... If only there were some Grilled Cassowaries ... 
You are pushing it, Captain. How about telling us what happened to this place?
Let's just get him what he wants. He is still kind of out of it.
Woot ... I love Grilled Cassowaries. It reminds me of Easter Day dinner at home!
Enough. Can you please tell me if you saw a lady with dark-brown hair and wearing a red sweater?
Lady, as in female? I haven't seen one of those in a long time ... 
What happened to this ship? Did anyone sent out a signal recently?
It was our mission to escort a team of researchers here. After they left the ship, a strange smoke enveloped the ship and turned most of us into monsters!
I have been trapped in this place. The Chief Engineer should be the one who sent out the signal. He should be in the Lower Deck. As for the lady, no, I haven't seen one on this ship.
If you are going there, I recommend you make some preparations; the monsters over there are not easy to deal with.
Are you ... Are you guys here to save us? How come there is a kid in the rescue team?
Why is everyone calling me that! Well, we are looking for someone. Have you seen a lady with dark-brown hair, wearing a red sweater?
No ... This place isn't safe. There are mutated bears all over the Lower Deck! I hope the person you are looking for is still alive ... 
Where is the Chief Engineer?
You must go through the cargos to get to him, but the path is being blocked by mutated bears!
Those disgusting creatures! You guys must prepare some better weapons to get past them!
Looks like you guys are ready for a fight. It's too bad that I don't have the strength to help. God bless you both ... 
Wow, you guys are still alive! How did it go?
