Well, okay, hold on a second, let me ... Bye!
Okay, okay, you found me, I give up.
Well, I've spent a lot of effort getting my hands on this perfume. I guess I'll give it to Cecile as my apology.
Would you mind give this to her? I'm afraid she's going to tear me to pieces if she sees me now ... 
This smell, I can't believe this really is a perfume, a very expensive kind too.
I can't believe Rothschild is being honest this time. What's he up to ... 
Well, I guess a perfume is good enough. Apology accepted.
I've checked what's inside the package. Mostly garbage except for one thing. Too bad you've spent so much time and effort on it.
Well, better than nothing.
That's true, if you run into any more packages like this one again in the future, don't hesitate to ask us to help you check it. This kind of thing is quite common here.
Make sure you don't just pick them up and leave them anywhere at the camp without having us checking them first. That could cause a lot of trouble!
Thanks for the reminder. I won't forget.
Where could it be...
Looking for something?
Yeah... My stuffed animals are missing, can you please help me find them?
There are four of them, a teddy, a bunny, a kitty and an elephant! They should be on the beach nearby but I just can't find them...
Do me a favor, young soul.
High quality gold nuggets were said to be found in the Shoal Region. If you can bring 20 of them to me you'll be well compensated. 
Already got them? Well done! Here is the rewards we agreed upon.
An extinguished campfire. This must've been used as a camp by someone...
This might be left by other survivors. I'll go look around, to see if there's any clue.
Aargh darn it! I used the last bit of paper to wipe my arse! Guess I'll have to write with some animal hides!
Yo Lucky! If you can understand human writings, congratulations! You've found the real treasure!
I am the expert survivor in the wilderness, the forest fox, the desert eagle, the alpha wolf, the lion king, the captain across the ocean, the dominator of the antarctic, the Island Gourmet - Ed Covington!
This island might be like hell for other survivors, but to me, this is the heaven!
Muahahaha! I'll let these creatures know they are now forced to live with me, not the other way around!
You might be thinking I'm insane, then you, my lucky friend, is completely mistaken! For I have left my conqueror's footprints well across this island!
C'mon baby! Witness the journey of the greatest conqueror - Ed Covington!
Woohoo! Took down a little boar ... This should be a boar right? Yeah it's got some strange stuff on its body, but judging from the test it's gotta be a boar!
By the way, tough wild animals like adult boars, are extremely dangerous to humans especially on this island.
That's why I always pick on the little ones! ... Of course I can deal with adult boars too, but piglets simply taste much better. After all I'm the Island Gourmet - Ed Covington!
(Hic) That was delicious ... I'll go sleep on the tree so I don't have worry about its parents!
Oh my god! There are giant crabs here! Look at this cutie! It's so big!
Woah! This one was actually pretty fierce! Look at those huge pinches! I'm loving it!
Sadly I can't enjoy this moment for too long. This cutie needs to be prepared quickly and carefully, coz I ain't gonna get a runny tummy from a spoiled smelly cutie crabby ...
Then there's this food poisoning possibility to worry about. Looks like I'll have to plan this out.
Aha! Coconut! Promise me you don't miss out on these if you see them!
Coconut milk is an excellent source of water, but you must make sure it's fresh ... Otherwise you aren't going to like your runny tummy, and the followed up dehydration problem!
Coconut milk is also an excellent container to store rain water. Coz I don't suppose you, or anyone, can find an intact glass bottles here!
Muahaha, time to pick up some coconut! I'm totally gonna end up making a castle with it!
Oh hey! Bananas! I knew all along this island is in the tropics!
This is a great source of sugar in the wilderness! I'm far from the only one who loves it, those monkey in the woods ... Jesus! They sure as hell love it more!
Well then, guess they are the perfect test subjects for the mighty stone hammer made by Ed Covington!
My coat ... connecting the zip ... Finally done!
Hold on where was I? Right, the bananas ... make sure you get the ripe ones, otherwise just don't blame me for your constipation.
Alright one more ... Delicious! So it's decided! I'm gonna sleep on a bed made of bananas!
Hey lucky! Still alive? Well if you get to see this journal, that means you've overcome all the difficulties in the Forest Region and successfully got to the swamp. I have to say, congratulations! 
But I gotta say, this swamp is even more dangerous. Just look at those flying bugs and the slimy mud puddles.
Even an expert like me had some missteps, and stepped straight into the slimy mud puddle. I ended up getting mud all over my boots, disgusting!
But the worst are those snapping turtles that will take advantage of you when you aren't paying attention. They will suddenly come out of the mud and bite you with its absurd jaws, which is capable of bending iron plates! Oh God! Had there be no protection, I would've ...
Although these snapping turtles have really sturdy shells, they're just not enough against a few hammer swings from the mighty Ed Covington! Come have some tasty grilled turtle, and you are in for a happy night!
Alright guess I'll call it a day. I'm just gonna wrap thing up by cleaning my boots, so it won't feel like I'm stepping on s*** all the time.
Best of luck! Lucky!
I knew I could find these here!
If you are asking me what they are, simple. Mushrooms!
In a tropical environment like this, you can find lots of mushrooms around dead woods. Simply take out the poisonous ones and you can eat all the others!
If you boil them together with meat, that meal will really stick to your ribs!
This is the moment when you might think, if we could really get bigger by eating mushrooms ...
Oh right, on an important note, unless you are an expert like me. Keep your mouth way from mushrooms in the wild, coz we ain't got no ambulance down here!
Holy cow! I can't believe what I've just found! We've got basil here!
You know this is a real treasure! Not just used as meds, but also for cooking!
Oh my ... It feels like I'm in heaven after having this ... stir-fried snapping turtle with basil!
It feel so good after not having any seasoned food for so long! I gotta collect more basils before I leave, coz who knows how long it'll take before I find other cooking spices or herbs.
Don't worry lucky, I'll save some for you. You should totally try cooking with it once you get the chance, it's just so awesome!
Jesus Christ! There are Crocodile in this swamp?
We all know crocodiles are ferocious predators. After undergoing mutations these ones are even more powerful and aggressive.
Lucky, if you spot an crocodile here, my best advice is, run as fast as you can!
They look dumb but once they've found a target, they can strike like lightning! And If you get caught by their jaws, I just hope your family has bought you the best life-insurance plan!
But I didn't need to run. I patiently waited for the perfect moment, and thrusted my spear from its opened mouth straight into its skull! Sounds easy but not recommended except for spear masters!
Then comes the difficult part. Crocodiles have really sturdy skin that's almost like some kind of natural armor. Apparently my kitchen knife wasn't working, so It took me ages to successfully slice it for cooking.
About the taste, honestly, this was my first time eating crocodiles and it was surprisingly good! It kinda tastes like a mix of chicken and a lighter version of pork. It's quite wonderful really ...
Hold on, I think just heard some noise from another crocodile! Looks like I'm gonna have a feast tonight!
After a few days of drifting, I can finally see land. It seems that the God still favors me!
The Terrain here is rather bizarre, and the temperature is also significantly slower. Perhaps I'm getting close to the North Pole.
There are lots of ferocious wild goats here that laid their eyes on me the moment I got here. Bad luck for them I gotta say!
I took them down easily, and they turned out to be such a delicious meal after being fully roasted! Don't miss out on them Lucky! 
Lucky! Guess what I caught here in this tiny puddle. You wouldn't believe I caught a beltfish would you!
Beltfish typically lives in the ocean. I even tasted the water in this little pond, and it's not even saltwater!
Can you imagine this? Beltfish living in freshwater! This place is insane!
But for now, nothing's more important than filling my stomach! Hopefully they taste as delicious as their pals in the sea!
Oh Lucky! I'm really surprised now. Can you believe I just saw a Cassowary that is supposed to live in the rainforests?
I was making a campfire for cooking, and suddenly its sharp claws struck from the shadow! Fortunately I reacted fast enough, or you wouldn't be able to see this journal.
This creature shouldn't have been able to survive under such a cold climate here, yet it did appear before me.
I'm actually getting a bit confused, but ... at least it tastes pretty good! It's even got an egg inside of it!
Catch one, get one free! What a great deal!
Lucky, have you ever imagined facing a crab larger than you? Would you be scared?
So it went like this, I was cooking the cassowary bundle, and suddenly THUD! That was a really loud sound!
As an adventurer, naturally I came to check out what happened. Then I saw a crab even taller than me, wielding its pinches around!
It actually took me a lot of effort to take down this crab. It had incredible strength and sturdy shell. My hammer was almost useless against it!
Crabs are extremely easy to cook. Simply boil it and it'll taste awesome! This one's even got incredible texture too! If only I could share it with you.
Oh I almost forgot, that thud sound was seemingly from a cruise ship crashing onto the shore. Time to check it out! Perhaps we'll even meet each other there!
I heard someone found Ed Covington's Journal in the Shoal Region. Would you kindly do me a favor to find it and bring it back to me?
You've found it? That's awesome! Can I have it?
It's late, how come the children are still not back
What happened?
My three kids have gone out to play but it's already dinner time. Can you please help me find them? They should be in the area north of Salvation Town.
Come on, can you go somewhere else? She's gonna find me if stay here ...
What are you doing?
We are playing hide and seek. Our sister is the seeker, and we are hiding.
Your mom's waiting for you to have dinner. She couldn't find you and was quite worried.
Aw... What about my brother and sister?
I'll go look for them.
Strange, where are they?
Your mom's waiting for you to have dinner! She's worried.
Well, we still haven't found them ...
Don't worry. We will.
Alright, but ... I didn't lose! Promise me you'll find them!
Why hasn't she found me yet ... I'm starving ...
Found you! Your moms waiting for you to have dinner, time to head home.
Dinner? Awesome! Let's go!
You've found everyone? Let's have dinner!
Wait mom, Mark isn't back yet.
Yeah right, where's Mark?
Can we start eating?
Hold on Andy, we need to wait for Mark to come back. Where could he be?
Mark? I saw him heading towards the Shoal.
Shoal? It's dangerous out there. I'll go look for him!
Thank you! We are all counting on you ...
You must be Mark?
Yeah ... I am. It's so scary here ...
Thank God you are alright? How did you get here?
I was playing Hide & Seek with my siblings, and I was simply looking for a place to hide, I didn't know ... Luckily she protected me.
She? Oh, that's you right? Thank you.
... (nod)
The mysterious lady left without a word.
What, she just left like this?
I don't know ... She doesn't seem to talk at all.
... Anyways. Glad you are OK, let's go home.
Oh thank God! You found all of them!
You're welcome. Don't forget about the time again the next time you guys head out and play! Especially Mark ...
I know ....
I'll make sure they don't run too far next time!
I'm hungry, can we start eating?
Here comes Sir Eats-a-lot!
Quiet kids, let's have dinner!
Thank you so much. Please take this as a gift, it is not exactly something valuable, but I hope you don't mind.
... There's something I want to say.
What's the matter?
... I don't think we can talk about it here, I'll wait for you at the beach, meet me there!
You are here...
Claire, you are wearing your old clothes now?
Yeah, I'm a descendant of Atlanteans, so I guess I should carry their legacy.
But as Jane's daughter ... the least I could do is to be who I was at this beach.
Oh, didn't think I would meet you here.
What are you doing here Herman?
I'm looking for some intact branches to fortify the camp fences. But as you see, I'm exhausted.
Sounds good.
I've already dug the fishing hole. but this damn cold wind is killing my old bones! Would you please help me catch a few fish for me? Trust me you don't want to miss out on my fish soup!
Here are your fish Herman.
Ahh, fresh fish! I'll get started started on cooking then. Come back and try this whenever it's ready!
Thanks but I'll pass. I've got something else at hand.
Oh well buddy ... Your loss.
You again Herman. What's up this time?
You know, I'm old and I can't really deal with the cold wind anymore. I was to look for some intact branches to fortify our camp fences. But as you can see, I'm exhausted.
Alright my man. You could've just asked in the first place.
Here are your frozen branches. I'll just put them in a stack here.
Wonderful! Thank you so much for bringing them.
Are you sure you can these branches back to the camp all by yourself?
Don't worry. I'm old but I've still got some tricks up my sleeves!
Oh hey! Look who's here! Such terrible weather ain't it?
Honestly I'm not sure which is worse, bad weather or you. Today must be my lucky day ...
Mwahaha! I know you are being sarcastic my friend. Look, I've got a great idea to add something extra to the camp at night, and the only things I'm missing are some ice crystals.
Just a few ice crystals? Alright I'll do it, but you'd better pay me well this time.
Here, your ice crystals. What about ...
Don't worry I know. I certainly won't have you work for nothing. Here, take this.
Well this looks good. Well Herman, the weather here is probably too harsh for you, so it's probably better if you get back to Salvation Town.
Thanks for your concern my friend, I'll be back soon.
