An offshore research organization accidentally released a biological organism that spread across the island and turned all its life forms into savage beasts ...
Human genetic engineering was the focus of the Offshore Research Union (ORU), and "Alpha" was the name of their initial experimental project. The original intention of any scientific study may be good, but this offshore organization can never imagine the consequence for their experiment ... and the disasters that followed ... 
Any modern biological studies cannot explain the genetic engineering study of the ORU. To avoid the risk of human experiments, natural biological researches were also carried out. This new experimental research was given the code-name, "Beta". Beta achieved many breakthroughs, but such achievements were not appreciated by mother nature.
"Log Number-Gamma 1006: The ruins were just like the legends told. What we found were not only high-end technology, but also containers that can keep the Atlanteans dormant, but we must wake up these ancient legends to mark a new chapter to our research." —Fishna Camo (Last Editor)
Code name-Delta. The laboratory with the most breakthrough genetic experiments, the fusion of cross-species genetic studies and ancient Atlantis technology, brought Delta's biological research to its "apex". To Lab Delta, humans and beasts are no longer two different words.
A mysterious place where the O.R.U keep their prisoners; it's heavily guarded. Then it was invaded by an Unknown Virus. The virus caused strange behaviors in all the prisoners and guards with some even lost their minds completely. After that, the O.R.U decided to abandon this place, and no one has heard any news of it ever since. But everyone should already know this place has become a living hell ... 
I don't know when this mysterious virus reached the ocean, but the ships in this place started to disappear. If you want to explore this place, then you must be careful; because, "When you stare at the abyss, the abyss is also staring at you" ... 
Ruins of the Atlantis; a battlefield for only the bravest warriors.
Thousands of years ago, the Mayan high priests, under the order of Saint Kukulkan, formed a large expeditionary force to cross the ocean to explore a mysterious archipelago. After landing on one of the islands, they found an ancient building in a forest. Inside it, the high priests sacrificed their prisoners to their god, then darkness soon came ... The entire expedition force went missing, and without these elite members, the Mayan civilization soon began to decline.\nThousands of years later, a few survivors on the island found the Mayan ruins and used the place to train elite warriors.
Complete Bounty Quests with other survivors to obtain a large number of materials!
There are many highly intelligent apes scattered on the ancient ruins. After discovering these creatures, the ORU quickly launched a research project named "Epsilon" and strived to use the similarity between the ape and human genes to create powerful creatures or soldiers that can be freely manipulated.
Some apes of the primitive tribe were willing to cooperate with the ORU for the benefits. The experimental project code-named "Zeta" was then established. The ancient technology hides the unimaginable mystery of human civilization, and ORU's ambition won't easily be dispelled.
ORU used "Eta" as the code name for a Mutant Cloning Experiment. For various reasons, the ORU temporarily abandoned the laboratory, but beware of what they left behind.
The ORU once studied "King Kong," the monster at the top of the food chain on a desert island. They sent many teams of elite soldiers to capture this beast, but none of them ever made it back home. But now, he is in ORU's crosshair again.
The ORU once studied "King Kong," the monster at the top of the food chain on a desert island. They sent many teams of elite soldiers to capture this beast, but none of them ever made it back home. But now, he is in ORU's crosshair again.
