Thousands of years ago, the Mayan high priests, under the order of Saint Kukulkan, formed a large expeditionary force to cross the ocean to explore a mysterious archipelago. After landing on one of the islands, they found an ancient building in a forest. Inside it, the high priests sacrificed their prisoners to their god, then darkness soon came ... The entire expedition force went missing, and without these elite members, the Mayan civilization soon began to decline.\nThousands of years later, a few survivors on the island found the Mayan ruins and used the place to train elite warriors.
In common sense, this crater has no particular strategic value, but the leader of the MIA, Baak, ordered his members to hold firm control over it. Baak believes this is where a great presence descends, hiding the ultimate mystery related to the remote island and its relationship with the rest of the world.\nBut after a specific incident, Baak gradually lost interest in this place, and the stationed MIA Soldiers gradually transformed it into a battleground for combat training.\nThey threw the captured Mutants, beasts, and sometimes powerful mutated behemoths into it, watching and killing them for enjoyment. Often before the end of the battle, soldiers would walk straight into the field to take part in the fight among the monsters.\nThe last person standing is the true warrior!\nOver time, this place became a trial place for MIA Soldiers to train new recruits, and Blood Ground became its new name. The proud soldiers even issued a declaration to the desert island: Only through trials on the Blood Ground can they be qualified to talk to a member of the MIA.
In 1990, Dean Solomon, a genetic engineer, chose to follow the voices in his head. He and the three disciples landed on the remote island and established a facility, the Genetic Research Lab with the help of mercenaries.\nUnder Solomon, a large number of experimental subjects were used for researching genetic modification. After making breakthroughs after breakthroughs, the once unthinkable idea of immortality was well within his grasp. \nYet he turned away for he would never let such research befoul his soul beyond salvation. \nAt the end of 1991, on the eve of the final experiment, Dark Fog quietly ascended. All the ambitions in the confinement center were burned to ashes, leaving only scaly claws ... 
Ten years ago, a team of science researchers observed a spatial curvature variation phenomenon and sent a team to investigate. At the heart of the curvature fluctuations, the team found a singularity in space. It was such an astonishing discovery even for this miraculous island! The team allocated a huge amount of resources to build a gigantic experimental facility around this singularity. The subsequent numerous experimental data and key technological breakthroughs directly proved that this decision was correct. \nJust when everyone was so excited, something happened, the nature of the space singularity was gradually changing, and the entire experimental facility disappeared in a blink. \nTen years later, this experimental facility resurfaced at the same place. The space of the whole facility became extremely disordered inside those motley walls. The spatial relationship between rooms was constantly changing. This facility that once fostered many breakthroughs and exciting discoveries has now become dangerous and uncharted territory.
The existence of this mysterious Lab 0 is only known by a few ORU members; The truth of the Mutation within the Lab has already been burried deeply in the history.
A biological laboratory located next to the ORU base. It was closed down for unknown reasons until recently when it was reinstated. According to a report by the ORU advance team, there appeared to be a few incidents related to the disorder of time and space ... 
Developing a type of invincible machinery warrior has always been the main focus at Lab Iota. The goal was to fully mechanize human soldiers. By combining the miraculous technologies of Atlantis, these mad scientists have conquered countless modern technical problems. However, the failure of this "machinery warrior" program has only proved one thing: messing around with unfamiliar technologies doesn't end well 99 times out of 100. 
The founding of Lap Kappa was deeply entangled with top secrets in early days of ORU history. It is actually where the major disagreement originated and developed. As the leading figures of the research team, Alma, Erick and Jane used to trust each other wholeheartedly. Together they managed to survive through countless crisis. Now Jane is fell into eternal slumber under the Valley, while Alma and Erick have completely parted their ways ... 
Many survivors claim to have seen the Northern Lights on the island, which in fact was created by something from the ORU Lab Lambda in the Highland. No one has yet to figure out what kind of equipment created something so majestic, and everyone who entered Lab Lambda for investigation eventually lost contact with the outside world - a fate shared even by ORU's own investigation team ...
Lab Mu was a research institute established by the ORU deep in the highlands, specializing in the study of all kinds of bizarre creatures on this island. However, after Alma changed the priority of the ORU, Lab Mu quickly altered its direction towards weaponizing those creatures, turning the lab into an place of incomprehensible misfortune.
Established in the deepest part of the Highlands region, Lab Nu is the most mysterious of all the ORU Labs, and it is said that many of the mysterious techs of the ORU came from here. Meanwhile, Lab Nu is also one of the first ORU Labs to close itself, and the people involved were extremely secretive about the cause ...
The ORU Arena hosted by Kane was meant to select the warriors to protect the Salvation Town against a greater threat in the future...
Numerous laboratories were established by the ORU on this island. There they used natural life, ancient civilizations, and space-time turbulence as objects of experiment.
