1. Registration and matchmaking: Registration is required to participate in the event. Registered camps will be randomly assigned to team blue or team red, and then grouped based on camp power. \n2. Stages: The event consists of two stages, gathering stage and combat stage. \n3. gathering Stage: The gathering stage lasts for two days, you can help Kane hunt down monkeys, defeat mutant leaders at the Lumber Mill and the Quarry to earn various rewards. you can also compete for resources in the Lumber Mill and the Quarry and hand them over to the Engineer or the Coordinator to improve the attributes of watchtowers, crystal, siege vehicles and player characters, thus making your side more effective in battles. \n4. Battle stage and victory rules: The battle stage takes place on Sunday. You need to follow and protect the siege vehicle to destroy enemy watchtowers and crystal, while protecting yours. \n5. Siege vehicles: These vehicles deal massive damage to enemy watchtowers and crystal, but they are very fragile, and thus must be protected. Siege vehicles respawn once an hour, and the timer is displayed on the event main menu. \n6. Crystal and victory: The key to victory is to destroy the enemy crystal. If neither side manages to achieve this, then the side with higher remaining crystal HP will be victorious. \n7. Watchtowers: You side must destroy at least one watchtower before the enemy crystal can be attacked. Each destroyed watchtower also weakens the attributes of the crystal. \n8. Camp reward: There are two types of camp rewards: participation reward for any camps that participated, and victory reward for camps that won in the battle stage. The rewards will be sent to your mailbox unless you did not earn any points in the Season Battlefield. \n9. Top 10 survivors on the elimination leaderboard will get elimination rewards sent to their mailboxes.
