1. Battle Reward: Defeat the monsters inside the Ancient Training Ground to receive a large amount of <color="#fee685">Character XP</color>.\n2. XP Limit: there's a limit for how much XP you can gain from the Ancient Training Ground. Once this limit is reached, you will have to <color="#fee685">wait for the refresh that happens after the countdown to gain more XP</color>.\n3. Battle Rules: There will be many buffs and firearms in the Training Ground. <color="#fee685">These firearms, buffs, and bullets will be taken back once you leave the Ancient Training Ground</color>.
Entrance:\nThere are limited attempts per day to enter which <color="#fee685">reset at 00:00 UTC</color>. \nCombat Rules: \nSolo only, choose an opponent to start the challenge, <color="#fee685">a maximum of 4 companions</color> are allowed on each side.\n<color="#fee685">Potions and certain other items cannot be used in the Arena, nor can you swap weapons</color>.\nVictory is achieved through defeating the opponent, or having higher amount of HP than your opponent when the timer ends.\nBeing disconnected during a challenge will count as a defeat.\nVictory will result in a rank swap assuming your opponent previously had higher rank than yours.\nRewards\nChallenge Reward: You get a victory reward from each victory, and a defeat reward from each defeat.\nDaily Ranking Reward: Daily Ranking Rewards are calculated on 00:00 UTC every day and must be claimed manually. Unclaimed rewards can be accumulated for up to 3 days.
Moving Maze Rules
1. Entry Rule: Only one person can enter; entry times <color="#fee685">are unlimited</color> each day. \n2. Battle Rule: Receive the <color="#fee685">Buff Card</color> by clearing all monsters in the room. You can choose the preferred<color="#fee685">Special Buff</color> that's available to be used in the Maze. \n3. Buff Rule: Cards level are ranked based on four Card colors:<color="#fee685">Green, Blue, Purple, Orange</color>. The darker the color, the stronger the buff effect. \n4. Unlock Method: Complete the current Floor<color="#fee685"> to unlock the next Maze Floor</color>. \n5. Moving Rule: After clearing all the monsters in the room, enter<color="#fee685">the Green Moving Block</color> to move to next room. \n6. First Time Completion Rewards: You will receive <color="#fee685">the First Time Completion Rewards</color> upon first time completion; the rewards will be sent to your <color="#fee685">Mail</color>. \n7. Completion Reward: You will receive the <color="#fee685">Battle Reward</color> in Mail once you have eliminated a Mutant Leader for the first time each day. You can only claim the reward only once per day (i.e. even if you've defeated more than one Mutant Leader at different Floors in a day, you'll only receive the reward after defeating the first one). Resets at 00:00 UTC.
