Skill Description:\nReckless charge- BF Mutant will charge up and then dash forward. At the end of the dash, BF Mutant will stun itself and greatly increase the damage it receives.\nConsume- When BF Mutant's HP gets low, it will go to the center of the field to consume the corpses to restore its HP. The recovery process will be interrupted when hit by a skill that can stun.\n\nBackground story:\nA powerful ancient race imprisoned by the people of Atlantis. Affected by the Dark Fog, his skull was hardened, which granted him extraordinary defensive power.
Skill description:\nShark Minions- The fallen priest will summon his Shark Minions to assist in the battle. In higher difficulty levels, the Shark Minions will tear your wounds and make you bleed to death! But the Shark Minions themselves are very vulnerable, and you can use AOE damage to destroy them.\nHealing Machine-the fallen priest will summon the healing robot of Atlantis when her HP gets low. The robot will continuously restore the priest's HP, so it would be best to destroy it first! \n\nBackground story:\nA priestess of Atlantis, who was consumed by Dark Fog and had her mind corrupted. She soon became one of the most dangerous beings in the land, along with the minions she summons to ambush her prey.
Skill Description: \nMirror Image— Primate Samurai summons his clone to assist in battles when his life is threatened. The clone is much weaker than his actual body. You can use AOE damage to destroy all of them. \nQuick Slash- Primate Samurai will enter a state of drawing his sword and slash his enemies, during which it will forcefully counterattack the enemies that attack him, but if no one attacks, he will stun himself after a period of time. \n\nBackground story:\nIt's said that the Primate Samurai was created by the scientists of the ORU who copied the Gene strands of a Japanese samurai. 
Skill Description: \nRebirth-Even in death, one of the Savage Mechasaur will not give up. If the other Savage Mechasaur is still alive for the next few moments, it will use its power to resurrect its dead companion! So you must defeat both of them at the same time!\nEnergy Transfer-The two mechasours will transfer power between each other. The receiving party will have a reduction in damage taken while the giving party will have an increase in damage taken. Take this to your advantage and you should be able to defeat them in no time.\n\nBackground story:\nORU used an incomplete dinosaur Gene and combined it with mechanical technology to create this pair of savage monsters. If only one is killed in battle, the other will use its power to revive its dead companion.
Skill Description:\nOil Bomb- Beetle Knights will periodically toss oil bombs that cause the ground to burn and deal sustained damage.\nDevour- When their beetle dies, Beetle Knights will jump off of it and keeps battling. They then will devour the dead beetle to restore their HP.\nBeetle Charge- The beetle will stay still to store energy then charge in the designated direction to deal damage. \n\nBackground story: \nThe beetle was a genetic verification of the ORU that roamed around in the wilderness. It was later domesticated as a mount by the ape tribe. The knights were selected within the tribe based on ranking. The combination of the two became the decisive and powerful force among tribal conflicts.
Skill Description: \nRolling Attack - the Chimera Dinosaur curls up periodically and rolls towards the target to attack \nWild Spit - the Chimera Dinosaur spits out three slimes that deal poison damage to the enemies that have touched the slime \nVenom Spin - under high difficulty, the Chimera Dinosaur will start spinning and spitting out venom at the same time to deal a large amount of damage and inflict poison effect. \n\nBackground story: \nThe Chimera Dinosaur is one of the creations of the Creature-Fusion Project developed by the ORU. It is a mixture of the genes of the dinosaur and a type of ancient venomous insect. There are venom glands hidden all over its body. The toxins contained in the venom could be lethal to its enemies.
Skill Description: \nEyes of Mutation - Nightwings will open its eyes on its shoulders and release a dazzling light after building up its strength. Players facing Nightwings will be stunned, turn your back to Nightwings to avoid being stunned. \nWhen Nightwing's HP drops below 50%, it will rise up in the air and attack the player with spikes from above, the player can use its spikes to knock Nightwings back down from the air! \n\nBackstory: The guardian created by the Atlantean civilization, although its flesh was corrupted by the Dark Fog over the long years, it's still fulfilling its duty.
