Proceed to Companions
1. After obtaining a new mount, you can activate it in the Mount Codex, which will reward you with rating points from the corresponding mount type. \n2. Gaining rating points will grant various bonus attributes. \n3. The amount of rating points gained when you activate Mounts in the codex are based on their quality. Divine, Legendary, Epic, and Superior ones are worth 30, 12, 6, and 2 rating points each respectively. \n4. When upgrading, modifying, and evolving mounts, you get progress points, which can be converted to rating points once you have a certain amount. \n5. The points and attributes from this feature are unaffected by whether the mounts are in the active slot or not.
1. After obtaining a new companion, you can activate the companion in the Companion Codex, which will reward you with rating points from the corresponding companion type. \n2. Gaining rating points will grant various bonus attributes. \n3. The amount of rating points gained when you activate Companions in the codex are based on their quality. Divine, Legendary, Epic, and Superior ones are worth 20, 12, 6, and 2 rating points each respectively. \n4. When promoting the star levels of companions, you get progress points, which can be converted to rating points once you have a certain amount. \n5. The points and attributes from this feature are unaffected by whether the companions are active in combat or not.
