Survivor Tip: Hive Annihilation
Dear Survivor: \nDon't forget to challenge bosses in Hive Annihilation as you grow in power! Doing so successfully will reward you with various materials, and the survivors who progressed the furthest will be placed on the leaderboard. \nTo enter, tap the Activity Overview from the top right, and you will find Hive Annihilation under the Challenges section.
Survivor Tip: Joint Hunt and Gear Modules
Dear Survivor: \nDo you want attributes that are not affected by switching your gears? Check out the Gear Modules, a great feature that allows you to roll for various random attributes to empower your play style. \nVarious modules and their enhancement materials can be found in Joint Hunt, a mode where you can fight along side your friends and allies. \nTo enter, tap the Activity Overview from the top right, and you will find Joint Hunt under the Challenges Section.
Survivor Tip: Moving Maze
Dear Survivor: \nA mode where you select a buff from 3 randomly chosen ones out of a total pool of over 20 buffs, find the best way to mix them up and defeat one powerful boss after another in the Maze. It's a great way to start you day in LOST in BLUE.\nTo enter, tap the Activity Overview from the top right, and you will find Moving Maze under the Dailies Section.
Survivor Tip: Abandoned Alchemy Lab
Dear Survivor: \nChallenge one powerful boss after another on a weekly basis. Whoever dealt the most damage will be placed on top of the leaderboard and earn admiration from all survivors. The Abandoned Alchemy Lab is also a fantastic place to obtain various materials used for crafting gears.\nTo enter, tap the Activity Overview from the top right, and you will find Abandoned Alchemy Lab under the Dailies Section.
Survivor Tip: Season Battlefield
Dear Survivor: \nThe Season Battlefield is where you strategize and flight along side your allies from the Camp Alliance for glory and rewards.\nAll members from top ranked camps will receive Refine Tool(s), Legendary Companion Fragment(s) as well as other rare rewards. \nTo enter, tap the Main Menu and select Camp, the Season Battlefield menu is displayed on the top right of the Camp Menu, in a rotation with Apex Arena.
Survivor Tip: Daily Arena and CPU
Dear Survivor: \nUnlocking and upgrading nodes at the CPU in the Island Terminal is a great way to increase your power. \nIt's typically more efficient to prioritize on unlocking nodes once you reach the prerequisite, and upgrade them later on.\nIn Daily Arena, you can earn Bionic Data, which is used for upgrading nodes in the CPU, and other rewards by defeating various opponents.\nTo enter, tap the Activity Overview from the top right, and you will find Daily Arena under the Dailies Section.
Survivor Tip: Main Quest
Dear Survivor: \nProgressing the main storyline not only helps you understand this lost island, but also grants you large amount of XP, and unlocks various additional features. Thus it's typically a good idea to prioritize on main quests when they are available.
Survivor Tip: Repair the Excavator
Dear Survivor: \nHere are some materials required for repairing the Excavator to help you speed up the process!
Survivor Tip: Codex
Dear Survivor: \nCodex for Mounts and Companions are now available. \nWhenever you obtain a new mount or companion, you can activate its corresponding codex. Doing so increases your rating in the category, which in turn grants you lots of attribute bonuses. \nTo enter, tap the Island Terminal from the main menu on the right.
Don't be discouraged!
Dear Survivor: \nLost a Hive Annihilation round? Don't be discouraged!\nTake these materials, and increase your power in various sections including gears, mounts, companions from the main menu on the right, and challenge again once you are powerful enough!
Survivor Tip: Deathmatch Battlefield
Dear Survivor: \nDeathmatch Battlefield is on! \nFight against other players in the battlefield to earn Deathmatch Points! \nTo enter, tap the Activity Overview from the top right, and you will find Deathmatch Battlefield under the Dailies section.
