Island Conquest · Qualifier
<color=#fee685>Details: </color>\n1. The world map is divided into 10 territories. <color=#fee685>Level 1 Territories: </color>Camp Region,  Island Region, Shoal Region, Glacier Region, Volcano - Peninsula Region, Volcano - Vent Region. <color=#fee685>Level 2 Territories: </color>Wasteland Region, Valley Region, Highland Region. <color=#fee685>Level 3 Territory: </color>Core Region. \n2. The conquest for territories of different tiers starts at different time within the duration of the event. In <color=#fee685>Stage 1</color>, Level 1 Territories become available for conquest. The top ranked camp based on Advancement Points ranking in each of the 6 Territories will advance to the next stage. In <color=#fee685>Stage 2</color>, Level 2 Territories become available for conquest. The top ranked camp based on Advancement Points ranking in each of the 3 Territories will advance to the next stage. In <color=#fee685>Stage 3</color>, Level 3 Territory become available for conquest, and the winning camp will be determined based on Advancement Points. \n3. <color=#fee685>Advancement Points</color> and <color=#fee685>Personal Redeem Points</color> can be earned during the event. The former one is camp based and is used for determine camp ranking in the event. The later one is used for redeeming various items from the event shop. We recommend using your Personal Redeem Points before they are reset to zero when the event ends. \n4. <color=#fee685>Event Restrictions: </color> Players who are not part of a camp cannot participate. \n5. <color=#fee685>Camp operation restrictions:</color> During Territory Conquest periods, you can join or leave camps at will, but you cannot disband camps. Warning: You will lose all your captured footholds if you leave your current camp! \n6.<color=#fee685>Auto Declare War: </color>When the Auto Declare War option is checked, if your camp has not declared war 12 hours into a stage, it will automatically do so against a camp.
<color=#fee685>Details: </color>\n1. The world map is divided into 10 territories. <color=#fee685>Level 1 Territories: </color>Camp Region,  Island Region, Shoal Region, Glacier Region, Volcano - Peninsula Region, Volcano - Vent Region. <color=#fee685>Level 2 Territories: </color>Wasteland Region, Valley Region, Highland Region. <color=#fee685>Level 3 Territory: </color>Core Region. \n2. The conquest for territories of different tiers starts at different time within the duration of the event. In <color=#fee685>Stage 1</color>, Level 1 Territories become available for conquest. The top ranked camp based on Advancement Points ranking in each of the 6 Territories will advance to the next stage. In <color=#fee685>Stage 2</color>, Level 2 Territories become available for conquest. The top ranked camp based on Advancement Points ranking in each of the 3 Territories will advance to the next stage. In <color=#fee685>Stage 3</color>, Level 3 Territory become available for conquest, and the winning camp will be determined based on Advancement Points. \n3. <color=#fee685>Advancement Points</color> and <color=#fee685>Personal Redeem Points</color> can be earned during the event. The former one is camp based and is used for determine camp ranking in the event. The later one is used for redeeming various items from the event shop. We recommend using your Personal Redeem Points before they are reset to zero when the Cross-Server Conflict ends. \n4. <color=#fee685>Event Qualification: </color> Camps that qualified for Stage 3 in the Island Conquest in this server, and the top 3 camps from the Island Conquest · Qualifier can participate in the Cross-Server Island Conquest. \n5. <color=#fee685>Camp operation restrictions:</color> During Territory Conquest periods, you can join or leave camps at will, but you cannot disband camps. Warning: You will lose all your captured footholds if you leave your current camp! \n6.<color=#fee685>Auto Declare War: </color>When the Auto Declare War option is checked, if your camp has not declared war 12 hours into a stage, it will automatically do so against a camp. \n7. Exclusive active skills for divine companions are unavailable in this mode.
<color=#fee685>Details: </color>\n1. All camps can participate in the Island Conquest · Qualifier in their own server. \n2. Top 5 camps from the Camp Advancement Point Leaderboard will qualify for the next round of cross-server conquest.
