<color=#fee685>Details for Territory Conquest: </color>\n1. Any camp in any given server can participate  as long as the camp leader or elders declare war. A camp can only be at war against one territory at a time.\n2. <color=#fee685>Foothold categories: </color>Combat Foothold, Chest Foothold, and Blocked Foothold. Blocked Footholds cannot be captured. \n3. <color=#fee685>Foothold Mechanics: </color>Footholds can be captured from the edge of the map to the center, you can only capture a Foothold if any member from your camp has captured one of the six nearby Footholds. \n4. <color=#fee685>Capturing Footholds: </color> Footholds can be captured through successfully defeating the monsters and opening the chest. After that, you will be stationed in the Foothold. Players from other camps can attempt to conquer this Foothold, if successful the Foothold will be stationed by them instead. \n5. <color=#fee685>Foothold Production: </color>A Foothold will start producing two kind of points after being captured, namely Camp Advancement Points and Personal Redeem Points. Different Footholds can have different production rate. \n6. <color=#fee685>Points Calculation: </color>Points are produced once every 10 minutes, or when a player from a different camp captures the Foothold. \n<color=#FF0000>Point Production Rate increases over time as the event progresses.</color> \n7.<color=#fee685>Cost to Capture: </color>Capturing Footholds costs Operation Points, which are refilled at 00:00 every day. Additional points can be purchased with Crystals. \n8. <color=#fee685>Inspire: </color>Camp members can spend Crystals to grant Inspire buffs to all members for the day. There is a limit on how many times the buffs can be stacked per day. The buffs are reset at 00:00. \n9. <color=#fee685>Leaderboards: </color>After the conquest, Each of the six territories have its own leaderboard, and the top ranked camp on each leaderboard can advance to the next stage.
