<color=#fee685>Details for Level 1 Territories: </color>\n1. The 6 camps that ranked 1st in their level 1 territories will advance to this stage. War can be declared by the camp leader or elders at the cost of camp resources. A camp can only be at war against one territory at a time.\n2. <color=#fee685>Stronghold categories: </color>Outer Stronghold (numbered 1-8) and Inner Stronghold (numbered 9-12). Each Inner Stronghold has two connected Outer Stronghold. You can attempt to capture an Inner Stronghold after capturing an Outer Stronghold. The production of Inner Stronghold will stop if both Outer Strongholds are captured. \n3. <color=#fee685>Capture Stronghold:</color> The first camp that defeated the guarding monsters (solo or team) will capture the stronghold and can station the garrison. Players from other camps can challenge, if successful, will replace the previous capturer. \n4.<color=#fee685>Stronghold Production: </color>The production of Camp Advancement Points and Personal Redeem Points starts after successfully capturing a stronghold. The production rate may vary between strongholds. \n5.<color=#fee685>Cost to Capture: </color>Capturing Footholds costs Operation Points, which are refilled at 00:00 every day. Additional points can be purchased with Crystals. \n6. <color=#fee685>Capture Limit: </color> There is a limit of how many Stronghold a player can hold, the player must give up an already captured stronghold in order to capture another one if the limit has been reached. In a team, abandoning would not affect your teammates from capturing, but the cost will not be refunded. \n7. <color=#fee685>Leaderboards: </color>After the conquest, Each of the three Level 2 territories have its own leaderboard, and the top ranked camp on each leaderboard can advance to the next stage. \n8. <color=#fee685>Battle-Assist:</color> Added several Battle-Assist footholds to Main Footholds (Inner and Outer Strongholds). Battle-assist operations can be done by spending Operation Points. The max number of foothold you can capture every day is shared between Main Footholds and Battle-Assist Footholds. \n9. <color=#fee685>Battle-Assist Restriction:</color> If your camp have captured the Main Foothold, members of your camp can capture its Battle-Assist Footholds. If you lose the Main Foothold, its Battle-Assist Footholds will fall as well. \n10. <color=#fee685>Battle-Assist Earnings:</color> Battle-Assist Footholds only generates Personal Redeem Points, in addition to providing extra DEF buffs to their associated Main Foothold.
