<color=#fee685>Details for Level 3 Territories: </color>\n1. The 3 camps that ranked first in Level 2 territories will advance to this stage. \n2. <color=#fee685>Map Tiles: </color> You may capture Footholds and Spires. Foothold categories: Combat Foothold, Chest Foothold, and Blocked Foothold. Blocked Footholds cannot be captured. Spires: There are 3 Spire categories, each with different production rate. \n3. <color=#fee685>HQ:</color> There are 3 HQs. Each camp will be randomly assigned one of them at the beginning of the stage. \n  1) Each Camp has an HQ. If the HQ is secured, Footholds and Spires captured by members of the camp will function normally, and members can capture other map tiles. \n  2) HQ under siege: If you camp controls none of the 6 Footholds next to your HQ, your HQ will be considered under siege, and all production from captured Footholds and Spires will cease. \n  3) HQ lost: If remained under siege for too long, your HQ will be lost and your camp will be eliminated! So take back one of the 6 Footholds ASAP! \n4. <color=#fee685>Foothold Mechanics: </color>Footholds can be captured from the edge of the map to the center, you can only capture a Foothold if any member from your camp has captured one of the six nearby Footholds. \n5. <color=#fee685>Capture Details:</color> The first camp that defeated the guarding monsters (solo or team) will capture the Foothold and can station the garrison. Players from other camps can challenge, if successful, will replace the previous capturer. \n6. <color=#fee685>Cost to Capture: </color>Capturing Footholds costs Operation Points, which are refilled at 00:00 every day. Additional points can be purchased with Crystals. \n7. <color=#fee685>Production: </color> A Foothold or Spire will start producing two kind of points after being captured, namely Camp Advancement Points and Personal Redeem Points. Different Footholds can have different production rate. \n8. <color=#fee685>Capture Limit: </color>There is a limit of how many Stronghold a player can hold, the player must give up an already captured stronghold in order to capture another one if the limit has been reached. In a team, abandoning would not affect your teammates from capturing, but the cost will not be refunded. \n9. <color=#fee685>Leaderboard: </color> The champion camp of the server will be determined by Camp Advancement Point earned in this stage of the conquest.
