<color=#fee685>Overview:</color>\n1. In Fair Contest, your Survivor characters will no longer be used, and the attributes of characters in this mode are unrelated to Survivor attributes.\n2. In each run, accumulating 10 victories will count as a victory for that run. If you lose 3 times, the run will end early.\n<color=#fee685>Special Abilities:</color>\n1. Weapon-Specific Improvements: Depending on the selected weapon, weapon-specific improvement options will be provided before specific stages begin.\n2. Basic Abilities: Basic abilities can be purchased using Contest Badges. Each basic ability purchased will grant 1 to 2 corresponding Class points.\nAutomatic Refresh: Before each battle starts, the available basic abilities will automatically refresh 1 time if you have not locked the existing ones. If locked, it will not refresh.\nFree Refresh: A free refresh will be granted before each battle starts, allowing you to refresh the basic abilities once after use.\nCrystal Refresh: Once the free refreshes for each stage are exhausted, you can use Crystals to refresh. A total of 5 Crystal refreshes can be used throughout the run.\nRandom Refresh: Random refreshes will consume Contest Badges, refreshing basic abilities and granting an additional basic ability.\nQuality of Basic Abilities: As the number of stages increases within a single run, the probability of refreshing higher-quality basic abilities will increase.\n3. Intermediate Abilities: Each time Class points meet specific requirements, a corresponding intermediate ability option will be offered.\n<color=#fee685>Stage Victory and Defeat:</color>\nVictory: Defeating the target within the specified time is considered a victory for this battle, awarding Contest Badges and advancing to the next stage.\nDefeat: If the target defeats you, it is considered a defeat for this battle, deducting one defeat count, awarding Contest Badges, but you will remain in the current stage.\nDraw: If there is no winner or loser within the specified time, it is considered a draw. Draws do not deduct defeat counts, do not award Contest Badges, and you will remain in the current stage.\n<color=#fee685>Settlement Rules:</color>\nPoints will be added or deducted based on the number of stages completed when the run ends.
