1. In the event interface, you can select a companion for the left slot as the <color=#75d964>Projected Companion</color> as the one with progression being copied in the recast.\n2. You can also select a companion for the right slot as the <color=#75d964>Companion to Be Developed</color>.\n3. You must first select the <color=#75d964>Projected Companion</color> before selecting the <color=#75d964>Companion to Be Developed</color>.\n4. After selecting the right-side companion, performing Perfect Recast will synchronize <color=#75d964>Level</color>, <color=#75d964>Star Level</color>, and <color=#75d964>Affinity</color> with the left-side Projected Companion.\n5. Only companions of the <color=#75d964>same original quality</color> are allowed for Perfect Recast.\n6. The current <color=#75d964>Star Progress</color> of the left Projected Companion must be <color=#75d964>greater than</color> that of the right-side companion to perform Perfect Recast.\n7. The maximum development progression achievable via Perfect Recast is the companion's <color=#75d964>highest progression before Peak Breakthrough</color>, with max stats: <color=#75d964>Level 160</color>, <color=#75d964>12 Stars</color>, and <color=#75d964>8 Hearts</color> Affinity.\n8. If the left-side Projected Companion has undergone Peak Breakthrough, only the <color=#75d964>highest progression before Peak Breakthrough</color> will be recast. Post-Breakthrough progress cannot be recast.\n9. If the left-side Projected Companion’s <color=#75d964>Level</color> or <color=#75d964>Affinity</color> is lower than that of the right-side companion, the higher progress will be retained.\n10. Perfect Recast <color=#75d964>does not cause any changes or impacts</color> to the left-side Projected Companion’s current development progression.
