Rules Explanation:\n1. Map\nEach event contains three exploration maps, which will be unlocked sequentially as the event progresses.\n2. Clearance Goal:\nEach map has one clearance goal and several perfect clearance conditions.\n3. Reward Acquisition: Achieve the clearance goal to receive the clearance reward. Achieve both the clearance goal and all perfect clearance conditions to receive the perfect clearance reward.\n4. Continue Challenge: If you have completed the map but have not met the perfect clearance conditions, you can continue to challenge the map to achieve them. Once you have achived perfect clearance, manually end the challenge to claim the perfect clearance reward.\n5. Rechallenge\nCleared maps can be challenged again, but rewards already claimed cannot be obtained again.\n6.Initial Power\nAt the beginning of the event, your highest historical battle power will be used for participation. If your battle power is below 200,000, it will be calculated as 200,000.\n7. Floating Value\nEach map has an initial floating value, which will affect the actual exploration results.\n8.Failure Attenuation\nIf the tile challenge fails, the monster difficulty will automatically decrease.\n9.<color=#ff0000>After the event ends, all exploration tokens will be cleared! Please pay attention to the event time.</color>
