Extreme Purge
Event Cycle: Starts every Thursday and lasts until the following Wednesday. \nChallenge Rules: Survivors may challenge the highest unlocked difficulty or any previously cleared difficulty stage. There is no limit to the number of challenge attempts.\nDifficulty Rules: Successfully clearing the current difficulty will unlock the next level. Each time the event opens, the system will set the difficulty cap for that instance as the survivor's historically cleared highest difficulty + 10. Therefore, the maximum challengeable difficulty may vary among different survivors.\nClearance Rewards: In normal difficulty, defeating all bosses is considered a clear, and the corresponding clearance reward is issued. These rewards are not reset; the clearance reward for each difficulty can only be claimed once, permanently.\nQuick Purge: When a survivor's current Power is ≥ 2 times the recommended Power for a difficulty, that difficulty will unlock the Quick Purge function. Using it allows you to obtain the clearance reward without entering battle.\nRankings: A leaderboard will record the clearance points and maximum time corresponding to the highest purgeable difficulty.\nRanking Rules: A leaderboard will be active in each event cycle. Ranking is determined by a comprehensive evaluation of cleared difficulty, points earned, and clear time.\nEvent Quests: Completing specified quests within the event grants corresponding quest rewards. Each quest can only be completed once per single event cycle.\nAttribute Adjustment: In this event, certain survivor attributes will undergo a unified adjustment to ensure a balanced and consistent challenge experience.
